      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel scared about going to a hospital, but these symptoms can also be indicative of other serious conditions, like a stroke or a brain aneurysm, that need immediate medical attention. While some mild symptoms might be part of a migraine aura, arm weakness and sudden blurry vision are not typical and should not be ignored. It's critical to err on the side of caution and seek immediate medical help to ensure there's nothing more severe requiring treatment. If you absolutely must wait, please inform someone close to you about the situation so they can watch over you while you seek assistance. In the meantime, if you're not home alone, having a friend assist could provide additional safety while you collect your thoughts and gather some help.",
